  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "text": "Three animals that went to space before us.",
      "hold_after": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "fly1",
      "text": "First, fruit flies. In 1947, scientists launched them on a rocket over New Mexico."
    },
    {
      "id": "fly2",
      "text": "They flew more than 100 kilometers up, and came back alive. The first animals ever in space."
    },
    {
      "id": "laika1",
      "text": "Next, Laika. In 1957, this street dog from Moscow became the first animal to orbit the Earth."
    },
    {
      "id": "laika2",
      "text": "But there was no way to bring her back. She never came home."
    },
    {
      "id": "ham1",
      "text": "Finally, Ham the chimp. In 1961, he flew into space and pulled levers when lights flashed, to prove a person could work up there."
    },
    {
      "id": "ham2",
      "text": "He splashed down safe, and got an apple as a reward."
    },
    {
      "id": "ham3",
      "text": "Three months later, the first American followed him."
    }
  ]
